{title: Sing a New Song}
{subtitle: Psalm 98}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] | [Gm] | [Cm] | [F] |
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Cm] | [D7] |
| [Gm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Sing to the Lord a new [Cm7]song
[F7]For he has done mar[Bb]velous things
His [Eb]right hand and his holy [Cm]arm
Have [D7]worked salvation for [Gm]him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sing a new [Cm7]song, sing a new [Gm]song
Make a [D7]joyful noise to the [Gm]King
Sing a new [Cm7]song, sing a new [Gm]song
Let the [D7]whole earth [Gm]sing
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Let the sea roar and all that fills [Cm7]it
[F7]Let the rivers clap their [Bb]hands
Let the [Eb]mountains sing together for [Cm7]joy
Before the [D7]Lord, for he [Gm]comes
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Outro}
| [Gm] | [Cm7] | [Gm] | [D7] | ×2
| [Gm] | [Gm] |
